1
00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:09,030
Good morning.In the last few lectures I've been talking about the history of domestic building construction.
早上好，在过去的几堂课里，我一直在介绍国内房屋构造的历史。

2
00:00:09,040 --> 00:00:15,490
But today I want to begin looking at some contemporary,experimental designs for housing.
但是今天我想介绍一些当代的房屋实验设计。

3
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:22,580
So,I'm going to start with a house which is constructed more or less under the ground.
所以，我将从或多或少的地下房屋建造开始说起。

4
00:00:22,590 --> 00:00:33,320
And one of the interesting things about this project is that the owners - both professionals but not architects - wanted to be closely involved, 
关于这个项目的一件趣事是房主想要密切加入，他们是专业人士但不是建筑师，

5
00:00:33,330 --> 00:00:37,330
so they decided to manage the project themselves.
所以他们打算自己管理这个项目。

6
00:00:37,340 --> 00:00:45,160
Their chief aim was to create somethere that was as environmentally-friendly as possible.
他们的主要目的是把某处建造得尽可能的有益于环境。

7
00:00:45,170 --> 00:00:54,660
But at the same time they wanted to live somewhere peaceful - they'd both grown up in a rural area and disliked urban life.
但是同时，他们想住在宁静的地方，他们都在乡村长大，厌恶城市生活。

8
00:00:54,670 --> 00:00:59,180
So the first thing they did was to look for a site.
所以他们做的第一件事是找地点。

9
00:00:59,190 --> 00:01:04,570
And they found a disused stone quarry in a beautiful area.
他们在一片美丽的地方找到了一个废弃的采石场。

10
00:01:04,580 --> 00:01:12,230
The price was relatively low,and they liked the idea of recycling the land,as it were.
价格相对便宜，他们喜欢再利用这片土地的这个想法。

11
00:01:12,240 --> 00:01:21,480
As it was,the quarry was an ugly blot on the landscape,and it wasn't productive any longer,either.
事实上，这个采石场是这片风景区的败笔，它早就停产了。

12
00:01:21,490 --> 00:01:30,070
They consulted various architects and looked at a number of designs before finally deciding on one.
他们咨询了各类建筑师，看了许多设计后才最终作出决定。

13
00:01:30,080 --> 00:01:40,990
As I've said,it was a design for a sort of underground house,and it was built into the earth itself,with two storeys.
正如我说的，这是设计地下房屋，它建在地里，有两层。

14
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:51,540
The north,east and west sides were set in the earth,and only the sloping,south-facing side was exposed to light.
北面、东面和西面建在地下，只有朝南的斜坡曝露在阳光之下。

15
00:01:51,550 --> 00:01:56,620
That was made of a double layer of very strong glass.
它由双层强硬的玻璃制成。

16
00:01:56,630 --> 00:02:05,000
There were also photovoltaic tiles fixed to the top and bottom of this sloping wall.
斜壁的顶部和底部还装有光电的瓷砖。

17
00:02:05,010 --> 00:02:09,340
These are tiles that are designed to store energy from the sun.
这些瓷砖用于储存来自太阳的能量。

18
00:02:09,350 --> 00:02:16,680
And the walls had a layer of foam around them too,to increase the insulation.
而且墙的四周还有一层泡沫，用来增强隔热。
